**Fix Cart.total()**

`total()` throws a TypeError: inside the `function` callback, `this` is not the cart. Fix it. Don't change `check`.

```js
// Test driver: don't change.
function check(prices) {
  return new Cart(prices).total();
}

class Cart {
  constructor(prices) {
    this.prices = prices;
    this.sum = 0;
  }

  total() {
    this.sum = 0;
    this.prices.forEach(function (price) {
      this.sum += price;
    });
    return this.sum;
  }
}
```

